[TR][TD]Static analysis[/TD][TD]SpotBugs plus a PMD ruleset with a project-specific rule that flags blocking constructs[/TD][TD][I]gradle.yml[/I] ([I]-PstaticAnalysis[/I])[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Binary API compatibility[/TD][TD]all 7 public API modules compared against the last release; an unannounced break fails the build, removals need a 2-minor deprecation window[/TD][TD][I]gradle.yml[/I] (japicmp)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Dependency CVEs[/TD][TD]OWASP dependency-check fails at CVSS >= 4; every accepted finding needs written justification in the suppression file[/TD][TD][I]dependency-check.yml[/I], weekly and on dependency changes[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Release provenance[/TD][TD]CycloneDX SBOM, SHA-256 and SHA-512 checksums, GPG signatures, SLSA build provenance, and the acceptance-run evidence bundle on every release[/TD][TD][I]release.yml[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Runtime acceptance[/TD][TD]nightly multi-server devstack: 2 Velocity proxies, 2 lobbies, 2 backends over Redis, on Velocity + Paper + Folia + Fabric, Java 21 LTS and 25+[/TD][TD][I]devstack-acceptance.yml[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Encoding and docs[/TD][TD]tracked text files scanned for UTF-8 mojibake; the docs site builds from the same tree[/TD][TD][I]gradle.yml[/I], [I]docs.yml[/I][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]What I haven't finished.[/B] [I]rtp-core[/I] and [I]rtp-proxy-common[/I] are still under the 90 / 80 target on branch coverage. Their floors sit a point or two below the measured numbers, because a partially recompiled tree makes JaCoCo discard stale execution data and read low; the floors only ever ratchet upward. What's left uncovered in [I]rtp-core[/I] is concentrated in the platform bootstrap and dispatch seams a plain-JVM test can't reach honestly, so I'm closing those with runtime-attested coverage from the nightly devstack instead of writing tests that only exercise mocks. Spigot, NeoForge, BungeeCord, and non-LTS Java releases run fine but have no scheduled live CI suite, so the support matrix lists them as best-effort.

[B]Scope of these numbers.[/B] Coverage and mutation scores measure how thoroughly the tests exercise the code. They are not a bug-free claim, and they say nothing about feature correctness on your world, your generator, or your plugin list; the nightly devstack run and your own staging server cover that.

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]In-game menus[/B] - two books (Paper / Folia; chat-paginated elsewhere). [I]/rtp menu[/I] is the player side: teleport, or pick a region, world, or biome. [I]/rtp admin[/I] is the operator side: config editor with search, setup prefabs, region and MSPT/heap visualizations, scan control, diagnostics. Gated on [I]rtp.menu.admin[/I]. The book is a read-only UI with the same permission checks as a typed command, so there is no inventory-click exploit surface; a chest-GUI picker ships as a bundled addon for operators who want one.
[*][B]Regions[/B] - any number per world; shape (Square, Circle, Rectangle, Polygon), radius, center, curve weighting, vertical bounds, world override, permission gate, price. Vertical adjustors (Linear, Jump, Fixed) for sky islands, void worlds, Nether ceilings. [I]worlds.yml[/I] [I]override[/I] redirects a Nether or End [I]/rtp[/I] to a safe world.
[*][B]Per-player queues[/B] alongside the global queue ([I]rtp.personalqueue[/I]), so one player's bad luck does not starve another's teleport.
[*][B]Effects engine[/B] - particles, sounds, fireworks, potions, titles on every teleport phase, gated by [I]rtp.effects.<name>[/I]. The Rift addon under [I]addons/[/I] in the repo is a worked example.
[*][B]Per-region arrival schematics[/B] - drop a Sponge [I].schem[/I] named after a region into [I]plugins/RTP/advanced/schematics/[/I] and every teleport into that region pastes it centered on the landing spot. Decoded in-house, no WorldEdit required, claim-aware.
[*][B]Economy[/B] - charge per [I]/rtp[/I] (Vault), per-region pricing, auto-refund on cancel, [I]rtp.free[/I] bypass.
[*][B]12 claim integrations[/B] via the bundled claim addon - GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, TownyAdvanced, SaberFactions, FactionsBridge, HuskClaims, RedProtect, CrashClaim, KingdomsX, Residence. Claim checks run inside the async pipeline, not on the teleport tick. Add your own through [I]RegionVerifierRegistry[/I] with one lambda.
[*][B]PvP / combat-tag gate[/B] - off by default; refuses or delays [I]/rtp[/I] for players who recently dealt or took PvP damage. Native tracking, optional PvPManager / CombatLogX / Simple Combat Log integration.
[*][B]Movement-cancel, damage-cancel, invulnerability-after-teleport timers, landing platform with decay[/B], countdown and warmup messages.
[*][B]Cross-server [I]/rtp[/I][/B] - Velocity, with SQL / Redis reservation tokens and shared state (Pro) or plugin-messaging (both builds). Validated on the in-repo devstack: 2 Velocity proxies, 2 lobbies, 2 backends behind Redis.
[*][B]Auto-RTP on events[/B] - join, first join, respawn, world change, move, teleport ([I]rtp.onevent.*[/I]). Pro adds a login reserve cache so join-time teleports are served from a pre-warmed destination.
[*][B]Diagnostics[/B] - [I]/rtp info[/I]: queue depth and growth, pipeline latency percentiles, chunk-ticket leak rate, TPS/MSPT, database latency, per-region Folia table, generation success rate and top rejection cause. [I]/rtp visualization[/I] paints region and biome maps and bad-location heatmaps onto real map items. No metrics add-on needed.
[*][B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] - queue depth (total / public / personal), last-teleport coordinates, player status.
[*][B]Hot reload[/B] - [I]/rtp reload <file>[/I] (file optional), or [I]/rtp config <file> set k=v[/I] which saves and reloads.
[*][B]Command-block and console ready[/B] - the same parser handles player, console, and command-block callers.
[*][B]Docs in jar[/B] - the admin guide unpacks into [I]plugins/RTP/docs/[/I] on first run.
[*][B]API and addons[/B] - [I]rtp-api[/I] (pre / mid / post teleport hooks, region verifiers, config, scheduling) and [I]effects-api[/I]. Addons compile against [I]rtp-api[/I] only and load through the [I]RTPAddon[/I] [I]ServiceLoader[/I] SPI, so one jar runs on Spigot, Paper, Folia, Fabric, and NeoForge. Three bundled addons (GUI picker, claim integrations, Countdown reference) self-extract into [I]plugins/RTP/addons/[/I] on first run; those and the other addons in the repo (Rift, Group, Linear, Tether) ship with full source under [I]addons/[/I] as copy-paste starting points. Delete one from the folder to turn it off.
[*][B]Swappable SPI[/B] - server backend, economy, location validity, shapes, world border, PvP checks, region file format, commands.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]


[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#16A085]Install[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [I]LeafRTP-Pro-x.y.z.jar[/I] into [I]plugins/[/I] (or [I]mods/[/I]). Upgrading from the free build: replace the jar, keep the data folder.
[*]Start the server. A [I]default[/I] region is written for you.
[*]Type [I]/rtp[/I]. Change anything in-game via [I]/rtp admin[/I] or in the YAML under [I]plugins/RTP/[/I]; both edit the same state and reload at runtime.
[*][B]Size the region to your world.[/B] [I]radius[/I], [I]centerX[/I], and [I]centerZ[/I] live inside the region's [I]shape:[/I] block and are measured in [B]chunks[/B], not blocks - a [I]radius[/I] of [I]625[/I] reaches 10,000 blocks. A radius left in block-think looks like a broken plugin. See [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/configuration/REGIONS/'][B]Regions[/B][/URL] and [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/configuration/WORLDS/'][B]Worlds[/B][/URL].
[*]For SQL / Redis or a proxy network, fill in [I]advanced/database.yml[/I] and [I]advanced/network.yml[/I]. Both are inert until enabled.
[/LIST]

Start here: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/QUICK_START/'][B]Quick start[/B][/URL] and [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/site/intended-usage/'][B]Intended usage[/B][/URL].

[SPOILER="Commands, permissions, configuration files"]

[B]Commands[/B] (aliases: [I]/rtp[/I], [I]/wild[/I]):

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Command[/TH][TH]Description[/TH][TH]Permission[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp[/I] / [I]/wild[/I][/TD][TD]Random teleport to the default region for your current world[/TD][TD][I]rtp.use[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp region:<name>[/I][/TD][TD]Teleport to a named region[/TD][TD][I]rtp.region[/I] / [I]rtp.regions.*[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp world:<world>[/I][/TD][TD]Teleport within a specific world[/TD][TD][I]rtp.world[/I] / [I]rtp.worlds.*[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp player:<name>[/I][/TD][TD]Teleport another player[/TD][TD][I]rtp.other[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp biome:<biome>[/I][/TD][TD]Teleport to a chosen biome[/TD][TD][I]rtp.biome[/I] / [I]rtp.biome.*[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp centerx=<x> centerz=<z> radius=<r>[/I][/TD][TD]Ephemeral per-call overrides[/TD][TD][I]rtp.params[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp menu[/I][/TD][TD]Player book menu[/TD][TD][I]rtp.use[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp admin[/I][/TD][TD]Operator book menu[/TD][TD][I]rtp.menu.admin[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp info[/I][/TD][TD]Operator diagnostics[/TD][TD][I]rtp.info[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp reload <file>[/I][/TD][TD]Reload all configuration, or one file[/TD][TD][I]rtp.reload[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp config <file> view|set <k>=<v>[/I][/TD][TD]View or set a config key, then reload[/TD][TD][I]rtp.config[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]/rtp scan start|pause|resume|reset|cancel[/I][/TD][TD]Background spatial-memory crawl[/TD][TD][I]rtp.scan[/I][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Permissions[/B] (full set in [I]plugin.yml[/I]):

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Permission[/TH][TH]Default[/TH][TH]Grants[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.use[/I][/TD][TD]true[/TD][TD]Use [I]/rtp[/I] and [I]/wild[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.see[/I][/TD][TD]true[/TD][TD]Tab-complete [I]/rtp[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.free[/I][/TD][TD]op[/TD][TD]Skip the Vault charge[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.params[/I][/TD][TD]op[/TD][TD]Per-call overrides ([I]centerx=[/I], [I]centerz=[/I], [I]radius=[/I])[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.personalqueue[/I][/TD][TD]false[/TD][TD]Reserve a per-player pre-warmed location[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.onevent.*[/I][/TD][TD]false[/TD][TD]Auto-RTP on join / firstjoin / respawn / changeworld / move / teleport[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.admin[/I][/TD][TD]op[/TD][TD][I]reload[/I], [I]config[/I], [I]scan[/I], [I]info[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]rtp.*[/I][/TD][TD]op[/TD][TD]Everything[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Configuration files[/B] under [I]plugins/RTP/[/I]. Every file is hot-reloadable and editable in-game. The everyday files sit at the top level; things you author live in [I]definitions/[/I], rarely-touched tuning in [I]advanced/[/I].

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]File[/TH][TH]Scope[/TH][TH]Example keys[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]config.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Teleport behavior, menu renderer[/TD][TD][I]teleportDelay[/I], [I]teleportCooldown[/I], [I]cancelDistance[/I], [I]menu.renderer[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]safety.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Block / biome safety filter[/TD][TD][I]unsafeBlocks[/I], [I]airBlocks[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]economy.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Vault pricing[/TD][TD][I]price[/I], [I]priceOther[/I], [I]biomePrice[/I], [I]balanceFloor[/I], [I]refundOnCancel[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]language.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Locale selection[/TD][TD][I]language[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]definitions/regions/<name>.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Per-region shape, radius, center, queue, price, gates[/TD][TD][I]shape[/I], [I]vert[/I], [I]radius[/I], [I]cacheCap[/I], [I]price[/I], [I]requirePermission[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]definitions/worlds/<name>.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Per-world region routing and overrides[/TD][TD][I]region[/I], [I]override[/I], [I]requirePermission[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]definitions/effects/<name>.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Lifecycle effects[/TD][TD]per-phase effect definitions[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/database.yml[/I][/TD][TD]SQL / Redis persistence[/TD][TD][I]database.type[/I], connection settings[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/network.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Proxy / multi-server[/TD][TD][I]network.enabled[/I], [I]transport[/I], [I]routing[/I], [I]reservation[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/performance.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Tick budgets, queue caps, caches[/TD][TD][I]maxAttempts[/I], [I]syncAllottedTime[/I], [I]minTPS[/I], [I]loginCacheEnabled[/I][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/biomes.yml[/I], [I]advanced/blocks.yml[/I], [I]advanced/ttl.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Biome whitelist and weighting, block-tag catalog, spatial-memory expiry[/TD][TD]toggles and durations[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/logging.yml[/I], [I]advanced/metrics.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Log verbosity, runtime metrics[/TD][TD]toggles[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]advanced/messages/*.yml[/I], [I]lang/**[/I][/TD][TD]User-facing text ([I]commands[/I], [I]player[/I], [I]network[/I], [I]placeholders[/I], [I]system[/I]) and bundled translations[/TD][TD]message templates[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][I]addons/integrations.yml[/I][/TD][TD]Claim-plugin reroll toggles[/TD][TD][I]rerollWorldGuard[/I], [I]rerollGriefPrevention[/I], ...[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER="safety.yml token grammar"]

Six token shapes can be mixed freely in [I]unsafeBlocks[/I] and [I]airBlocks[/I]:

[LIST]
[*][B]Plain material[/B] - [I]LAVA[/I], [I]MAGMA_BLOCK[/I].
[*][B]Material + state predicate[/B] - a material followed by a bracketed predicate list. Multiple predicates AND together.
[*][B]Numeric range predicate[/B] - comparison operators inside the predicate. Fail-open on an absent or non-numeric value.
[*][B]Vanilla block tag[/B] - [I]#minecraft:leaves[/I], [I]#minecraft:fire[/I], [I]#minecraft:campfires[/I]. Expanded from the server's live block-tag registry at config load, so datapack and modded tags resolve too.
[*][B]Tag + state predicate[/B] - a tag followed by a predicate list.
[*][B]Wildcard + state predicate[/B] - [I]*[/I] followed by a predicate list; one line replaces the whole waterloggable enumeration.
[/LIST]

Predicates use square brackets, which this listing format cannot show literally; worked examples of every shape are on the [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/configuration/SAFETY/']Safety[/URL] page of the admin guide.

Unknown tags and properties fail open, so a config written for a newer MC version still loads on an older one. Malformed tokens are never silent; the log line names the file, the rejected token, and the reason. Block-state extraction only runs when a token needs it, so plain-material configs pay nothing. Plain-material entries from an older [I]safety.yml[/I] keep working unchanged.

[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER="Roadmap"]

[LIST]
[*][B]Fully-automatic self-warming[/B] - background spatial-memory accumulation without the [I]/rtp scan[/I] verb.
[*][B]Anonymous opt-in telemetry[/B] - reference benchmark sourced from real deployments.
[*][B]Chunky-driven scan generation[/B] - let a bulk pre-generator lay chunks down first, then scan reads them through the Anvil pre-filter.
[*][B]Leaner scan path[/B] - measure how accurately the pre-filter alone trims candidates and, where it is accurate enough, skip the full-load verification pass during scans.
[*][B]Accelerated scan compute (exploration)[/B] - offloading the bulk safety sweep to native SIMD, GPU, or an external generator, with a fallback to the current path.
[*][B]Native BungeeCord proxy adapter.[/B]
[/LIST]

File a GitHub issue if you hit something not on the list.

[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER="FAQ"]

[B]Q: Should I buy Pro or use the free build?[/B]
A: Free, unless you need one of the rows in the table above. The engine and the Paper benchmark are the same. Pro pays for SQL / Redis, the login reserve cache, the tuned Folia adapter, and a support response time.

[B]Q: Does LeafRTP work on Folia?[/B]
A: Both builds. The free build uses a correctness-first regionized scheduler that always hops to the owning region. Pro's adapter runs the pre-filter before the Region Scheduler so rejected candidates never hop, and teleports through the Entity Scheduler. On the unpaced Folia run above the measured difference is 13.2 vs about 12.5 TP/s; I expect it to widen under per-region contention but have not measured that yet.

[B]Q: How do I set up teleportation between worlds?[/B]
A: Resolution order: player's current world (or [I]world:[/I] param) -> world's target region -> region's target world. See the admin guide.

[B]Q: Do you support triangle / diamond region shapes?[/B]
A: Use the [I]Polygon[/I] shape. A triangle is a 3-vertex polygon and a diamond is a rotated square.

[B]Q: Do I need Chunky or another pre-generator?[/B]
A: No, but they work well together. [I]/rtp scan[/I] walks a region off-tick, verifies safety, and generates chunks that aren't on disk yet while recording which sectors are unsafe. Run Chunky first if you want the whole map on disk up front, and scan will read those chunks through the Anvil pre-filter instead of generating them.

[B]Q: Biome targeting on a pregenerated or upgraded world?[/B]
A: Biome data comes from the populated [I].mca[/I] files, so [I]/rtp biome:<x>[/I] reflects what is actually on disk, not what the current seed would generate. This is the case that trips plugins using the live noise-map lookup after a version migration.

[B]Q: Iris / Terra / custom datapack generators?[/B]
A: Yes. Region files are read directly, so modded and namespaced IDs are preserved. Un-populated chunks fall through to a live load.

[B]Q: Memory and MSPT - should I worry?[/B]
A: MSPT, no. Memory, know what you are buying: LeafRTP trades heap for tick time, on purpose. Every cache tier is capacity-limited; about 68 bytes per cached location in the hot buffers and about 26 bytes per known-bad chunk in the compressed spatial segments, so 8 192 cached locations cost well under a megabyte. Background generation pauses under heap pressure ([I]maxHeapPercent[/I]). If you are tight on RAM, lower [I]cacheCap[/I].

[B]Q: Can I downgrade to the free build?[/B]
A: Yes. Same configuration, same data files, same commands. Swap the jar; [I]advanced/database.yml[/I] and [I]advanced/network.yml[/I] become inert and SQL-backed state is not read.

[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER="Support"]

Support comes from the maintainer who wrote the code.

[LIST]
[*][B]Priority.[/B] Pro tickets are handled ahead of free-build tickets, and this is the tier on which early-access platforms and scaling backends are guaranteed.
[*][B]Response time:[/B] 24-72 h on weekdays. Critical safety issues jump the queue.
[*][B]Bug reports[/B] with server version, plugin version, platform, relevant configs, and log lines are resolved fastest. Most setup questions are answered in the admin guide.
[*][B]Feature requests[/B] via GitHub issues. Priority follows the published roadmap.
[*][B]Native NeoForge[/B] is supported on 1.21.x / 26.x. [B]Native Forge[/B] is not: use Arclight or Mohist with the Spigot/Paper jar.
[/LIST]

[/SPOILER]

